implementationPlan.description:
Launch-level tests in scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs. It holds one case list for both wrappers, run by postflight.sh with the sh engine and by postflight.ps1 with ps1. Register three new cases in the cases map.

Common fixture: repo() plus
- `big/` holding about 30 nested directories, each with its own .gitignore;
- `big/` and `.serena/` appended to <top>/.git/info/exclude only, which is the UnAI shape;
- a tracked src/.gitignore holding `*.tmp`;
- `.serena/project.yml` with project_name and `ignored_paths:` holding `- keep-me/`;
- an existing `.serena/project.local.yml` holding a user comment and `read_only: false`;
- knobs that pin XDG_CONFIG_HOME to a fixture dir, so no real ~/.config/git/ignore leaks in (HOME is already a fixture).

1. 'serena-ignore' (shared mode, like 'shared-landed': FAKE_CLAIM_WORKSPACE:null, MOE_SERENA_PATH:process.execPath, type claude):
   - after the launch, .serena/project.local.yml equals a LITERAL expected text: the user bytes unchanged, then the Moe block with `ignore_all_files_in_gitignore: false` and the ignored_paths "/.git", "keep-me/", the info/exclude patterns ("big/", ".serena/"), the root .gitignore patterns and "src/**/*.tmp";
   - the log has the [OK] MOE_SERENA_IGNORE_OVERRIDE line;
   - a second launch leaves the file's bytes and inode unchanged and logs the up-to-date line.
2. 'serena-ignore-off', each launch still running the CLI with today's exit code:
   - (a) no Serena: MOE_SERENA_PATH unset and PATH filtered of every dir holding a `serena` executable. No MOE_SERENA_IGNORE line, and project.local.yml is byte-identical.
   - (b) MOE_SERENA_IGNORE_OVERRIDE=0. File unchanged, plus the SKIPPED line.
   - (c) .moe-agent.json serenaProject pointing at a plain dir outside any repo. Nothing is created in it.
   - (d) serenaProject pointing at a dir whose .git file names a missing gitdir. Nothing is created in it.
3. 'serena-ignore-wt' (a worktree-mode claude launch): W/.serena/project.local.yml holds a block computed for W, and W/.serena/project.yml still carries WT-06's `project_name: ...@<task>` rewrite.

Check every existing case still passes. Fixture repos do not ignore .serena/, so the script skips there and must not change any compared tree. postflight-safe.mjs fails on a line that starts with SKIP, and our line starts with '[info] '.

Docs (DoD 4). Keep each to a few sentences.
- docs/MEMORY.md: add a short 'Serena startup ignore override' subsection under the Caveats section. It covers:
  - why it exists: Serena's startup .gitignore walk ignores .git/info/exclude and core.excludesFile and enters .git/. On UnAI, 112 info/exclude-d worktrees made every new seat's Serena time out for 15-23 min;
  - what each launch does: it runs scripts/moe-serena-ignore.mjs on the Serena root, which writes a managed block in .serena/project.local.yml only when git ignores that file. The block turns the walk off and lists the same patterns, converted as Serena converts them;
  - the fail-open cases;
  - how to opt out: MOE_SERENA_IGNORE_OVERRIDE=0, or setting ignore_all_files_in_gitignore or ignored_paths yourself in project.local.yml outside the block.
- scripts/CLAUDE.md: one sentence in the 'MCP servers for spawned agents' bullet (:43), next to the Serena resolution text, naming the script, both call sites (shared root and worktree W) and the opt-out.
- docs/CONFIGURATION.md: one env-table row after MOE_SERENA_PROJECT (:57): `MOE_SERENA_IGNORE_OVERRIDE` | `0` turns off the launchers' Serena ignore override | on | `0`.

Adversarial self-review of this diff (load the adversarial-self-review skill). Then run mutants in scratch copies of the snapshot's scripts/: copy the whole scripts/ tree per mutant and run an unmutated control first (mem:gotcha-postflight-worktree-mutant-copy). Run only the three new cases through MOE_WORKTREE_ONLY for each engine.

Mutants, each to be KILLED:
- M1: the sh shared call removed. serena-ignore (sh) must fail.
- M2: the ps1 shared call removed. serena-ignore (ps1) must fail.
- M3: the sh W call removed. serena-ignore-wt (sh) must fail.
- M4: the ps1 W call removed. serena-ignore-wt (ps1) must fail.
- M5: the call runs even when SERENA_CMD is empty. serena-ignore-off (a) must fail.
- M6: the W call placed before the tooling program. serena-ignore-wt must fail on project_name, or on the block's project.yml entries.

Checklist:
- set -e safety;
- PS 5.1 native-stderr handling under EAP Stop;
- a Serena root with spaces or a trailing backslash;
- concurrent seats writing the same file (the script renames atomically and writes only changed bytes);
- protected seats: the script reads MOE_PROTECTED_GIT, and skips until task-3acf7f79 exports it;
- the extra launch time, a few git calls.

Record the evidence under /mnt/d/moe-scratch/e3e81c45-work, and write the handoff memory task-task-e3e81c457c0e405a909cde910a2a8330-handoff.
